 "stick_limine_conf": "# USB live medium only; the ISO and installed disk configurations are unchanged.\n# px87 (pax#246): `quiet` (px15's word, kernel/user): the live session prints\n# no line for a program's ordinary life (its exec, its exit, a system call it\n# is the first to try that PAX lacks), so the screen holds what the programs\n# and the installer write; a refusal, a fault and a bad buffer still print.\ntimeout: 3\n\n/PAX live (root, no password)\n    protocol: limine\n    path: boot():/boot/pax\n    cmdline: quiet\n    module_path: boot():/boot/initramfs.cpio\n\n# px93 ([a ruling number, elided from this record]): the upgrade entry, chosen from the menu, never the\n# default. `pax.upgrade` and the stick's own /pax/install-targets as a\n# second module make kernel/fstab mount the listed disk's PAX root at\n# /mnt/target for `pax-install --upgrade`; the entry above mounts nothing.\n/PAX: upgrade the installed system\n    protocol: limine\n    path: boot():/boot/pax\n    cmdline: quiet pax.upgrade\n    module_path: boot():/boot/initramfs.cpio\n    module_path: boot():/pax/install-targets\n",
